<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύ-στᾰτος</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξ-, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνίσταμαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not solidified,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ ἀ. ὑπὸ βίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					61a
				</span></i>
			; <i>not cohesive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.949b
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>
			<i>want of cohesion,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				697a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάλα ἀ. εἰς τυρόν</span>”
				<i>that will not curdle,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CD</u>
					1.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>unformed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμβρυα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antyll.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.31.5
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>incoherent,</i> of Aeschylus, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1367
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>that cannot be composed, incurable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1467
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>incapable of subsistence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἀνύπαρκτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Stoic.</u>
					3.91
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Stat.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>irregular, inadmissible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				55.11
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<i>chaotic, confused,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1025a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>7.</b> of
			self-evident propositions, <i>incapable of proof</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύστασις</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> Aphr.<i><span class="en">
				<u>in Top.</u>
				84.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>8.</b> of legal
			status, <i>not determined,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				1680.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A. D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
